<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The camera screen: what to do next, and how well it is going.

  Translators: almost everything here is read at arm's length, in one glance, by somebody
  walking backwards round a room with a phone held up. Short wins over complete. The two
  halves of the prompt work together — `capture_room_*` is the state and
  `capture_room_*_hint` is what to do about it — so they should not repeat each other.

  Never soften the drift and closure wording. Telling a user their plan is worse than they
  think is the entire product position (docs/PRODUCT_PLAN.md §5); a translation that reads as
  reassurance breaks the thing the app is for.
-->
